  "name": "NORTHERN VIGIL",
  "forces": "Joint task group: Flight III Aegis, Ford and Queen Elizabeth, Type 45, FREMM, future Type 26, Astute, F-35B/C, E-2D, Merlin and Triton. Opposing surface, air and submarine forces; neutral merchant and fishing traffic.",
  "description": "Fictional 2030 coalition exercise. Coordinate two aviation groups through a Flight III Aegis console. Launch E-2D from Resolute and F-35B from Queen Elizabeth; the STOVL carrier cannot operate E-2D or F-35C. Deploy Merlin and the submarine screen against acoustic contacts. A Triton at the western field offers persistent radar surveillance but carries no weapons. Hold both carriers and the replenishment ship for 60 minutes. Deep submarines retain a local sensor picture: select their console to see what they hold. Neutral fishing traffic complicates identification. Type 26 uses a prospective fit; all scenario performance is estimated.",
